parts.text:
Note: When media source is set, `applyStringProperty` is called twice in `applyStyle` (explicit then inside), fine.

Now transport.ts inbound size and error counter. Add constant, field, checks. Need to be careful with Blob path: check after arrayBuffer conversion. Add `MAX_INBOUND_BYTES = 2 * 1024 * 1024`. But MAX_STRING_BYTES = 1 MiB; opcodes up to 1 MiB? 65536*16 = 1 MiB; total up to 2 MiB. Good.

Implement:
```
private protocolErrors = 0;
...
private handleMessage(data) {
 ...
 if (data instanceof ArrayBuffer) bytes = ...
 else if Blob... 
 else bytes = new Uint8Array(0)
 if (bytes.length > MAX_INBOUND_BYTES) { log.warn; this.protocolFailure(); return; }
 ...
 try parse; catch ProtocolError { this.protocolFailure(); return; }
 ...
 if (this.isSequenceGap...) { ... }
 ...
 try applyBatch; catch ProtocolError { this.protocolFailure(); return; }
 this.protocolErrors = 0;
 ...
}
private protocolFailure(): void {
  this.protocolErrors++;
  if (this.protocolErrors >= 5) { log.warn(...); this.protocolErrors = 0; this.ws?.close(); }
}
```
Need not close on sequence gap (not protocol error). Reset on successful apply. If parse succeeds but apply fails due to structural, count. If batch has unknown value type, apply fails.
Note: `handleMessage` for `Blob` returns before; okay.
If bytes length is 0 (non-buffer data), parse throws ProtocolError -> count. Fine.

Also maybe `location.reload` on version mismatch resets? no.

Edit.

